      "math_academy_id": "e-8141",
      "problem": "Find the domain of $g(x) = -2\\sqrt[6]{x+1}-2.$",
      "worked_solution": "The domain of $y = \\sqrt[6]{x}$ is\n\n$$\nx \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTo find the domain of $g(x) =  -2\\sqrt[6]{x+1}-2,$ we replace $x$ with $x+1$ in the above inequality. This gives\n\n$$\n{x+1} \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ x & \\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $y = g(x)$ is $x \\in [-1, \\infty).$ \n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=g(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14239886/assets/7eeaa091e1a1417efa5800abe3fd937c78957123c425c5a0d2ef239ca4994732.png)",
